      "remediation": {
        "description": "A DNS record points to a cloud resource that does not exist or is not owned by the organization. An attacker can claim the resource and serve content under your domain — phishing, malware, or credential harvesting that appears to originate from a trusted hostname.",
        "action": "Either claim the target resource in your cloud account to block takeover, or delete the DNS record that points to the unclaimed resource. Audit all DNS zones for records pointing to decommissioned infrastructure.",
        "example": "{\n  \"dns\": {\n    \"record_type\": \"CNAME\",\n    \"target_exists\": true,\n    \"target_owned\": true\n  }\n}\n"
      },
